        {
          "id": "note",
          "kind": "note",
          "data": {
            "text": "## Passive radar\n\nYou do not transmit. A broadcast FM station does, and this watches its signal bounce off aircraft.\n\n**Array** needs at least two coherent lanes: one antenna points at the transmitter for a clean reference, the others watch the sky. Set `reference_element` on the radar to whichever lane that is.\n\n**Passive radar** compares the two. What it subtracts is the direct signal and the ground clutter; what is left is the echo, and its delay and Doppler become a range and a speed.\n\n**GPS position** here is not your station. It is the **transmitter's** location, which the geometry needs to turn a delay into a position. Set it to a fixed point at the illuminator.\n\n**Map** draws the tracks.\n\nTune the Device to a strong local FM station. Strong matters more than close."
          },
          "position": {
